Many thanks to Rob Urban for answering this most clearly: since collect 
does not probe SCSI buses, there is no danger of SCSI resets.


 >collect doesn't probe the SCSI bus.  It reads the in-kernel data structures.
 >that's all.  That's why it doesn't see new disks until you actually access
 >them.
 >
 >Rob Urban

Original Message:

 >Has anyone run collect on clusters, particularly the Production Server?  I
