My Original Question:
 
> I have a problem with configuring the Operating System Selection Setup
> after upgrading the firmware on an ALPHA 255. 
> 
> I am running Unix Version 4.0F.
> 
> I get to a window that tells me I need to configure the Operating System.
> There are two options. "Windows NT" and "Primary Operating System", with
> an instruction that F8 selects Primary.
> 
> However F8 does nothing although all the other function keys do what they
> are supposed to.

> Can anyone help.
 
 
 The solution came from Joe Fletcher:
 
 Redo the firmware update but make sure you do UPDATE SRM as the last step.
This ensures you get the SRM console instead of the ARC you see at the 
moment.

Some Alphastations on have one console ROM instead of two so the will run
EITHER SRM or ARC but not both as most do. The AS255 is one of those 
systems.
 

