Hi Managers,

I asked:

> I obtained a strange problem: user A can't login from CDE login screen
> while user B can. Doing a login from user B's account to user A's
> account with ssh or rlogin works fine. This problem is specific to
> user A in the sense that the CDE login doesn't work on at least one
> other machine.
> 
> We are using NIS and home directories are NFS exported.

Thanks to 

Thomas Leitner <tom@radar.tu-graz.ac.at>

who solved the problem: 

    There was a bug in CDE login which prevents users to log-in who's
    usernames were exactly 8 characters long. If this is the case, you'd
    need to install a newer patch kit to get rid of it.

Thanks also to 

"Sheila Hollenbaugh" <shollen@cs.wright.edu>
scoates@resourcepartner.com
Knut.Hellebo@nho.hydro.com

for their responses.

I forgot to mention that I'm using Digital UNIX V4.0E with PK 2
on the machines I tested.

Thanks again
Gerhard

