The answers included using qpopper instead of the other pop3-server used,
writing a script and the right one:

Use poppassd (ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/IAS/poppassd.tar.Z), and make sure the

poppassd	stream	tcp	nowait	root	/usr/bin/tcbd
/usr/bin/poppassd	poppassd

line is in /etc/inetd.conf

