Dear friends, you are the VERY best all over the net!

I received many answers, and I succeded in using "robot" under
T64 v5.0 (1st patch applied, but I suppose it does'nt matter).

I first installed SCSI CAM (CLCMC500) which come in the Associated Product 
vol 1/2 and I had no problem. (using setld)
Then I installed MRU 1.2 (to be honest I simply copied an old 
/usr/opt/ROBOT120 tree on the new v5.0 system)

Then I followed the steps indicated by Bryan Cox (thanx!) which are:

1)	hwmgr -view		(to view all the devices connected to system) 
2)	dsfmgr -k		(To create devices special files for all the 
				  devices connected after system boot)
3) 	dsfmgr -K 		(To create device special files for all the 
				devices connected to system)
4)	scu scan edt 		(They serve the same purpose as before)
5)	scu show edt  
6)	hwmgr -scan scsi
7)	hwmgr -show scsi.

CLI Commands:
You can use all the CLI robot command

setenv MRU_ROBOT /dev/changer/mc0
robot show robot 

I've not been able to run xrobot since at startup it uses a file I
don't have: /dev/mc_mkdev (probably becouse of improper installation of MRU)

anyway, I succeded in using robot from T64 V5.0 !! 

Thanx again to our beautifull & usefull mailing list, 
greetings to all from Italy,

Emanuele


