------- Forwarded Message
The CLC3xx kits will NOT install on Tru64 V5.0.  If you must use the
CLC kit on V5.0, then you must install the CLC 5.0 kit.
The fact that it is unsupported does not mean that it will not work.
What it means is that it has not been tested very thoroughly.  If the
CLC 5.0 kit is installed on Tru64 V5.0, then you do so at your own
risk of the robot working or not.  For the most part, it will.
FYI, the CLC kit will no longer exist after the [unsupported] 5.0 kit.
As of V5.0A (not released yet), the changer driver is built into the
kernel without being a layered product.
------- End of Forwarded Message
What this means is that there is an "updated" CLC kit for use with
Tru64 UNIX V5.0 (I'm not personally sure where you'd get it), and
we are working on integrating the support for the devices that were
supported by the CLC kernel components in old releases directly in
the V5.0x product, with the first release due as part of V5.0A (and
that should be out before summer in the northern hemisphere, but I
won't try to give you a firm date; it is in field test already and
we are working to get it out soon).
So, if I were you, I'd wait for V5.0A before trying to upgrade.  If
you are concerned about support for V4.0D, you can either update to
V4.0F (or to V4.0G, but that will come out after V5.0A if things go
as we expect), and then go to V5.0A (or a later V5.x based release)
when you are ready.  In any case, V4.0D is fully supported and will
be supported at least into the year 2001.
