Hi Managers,

I asked:
> I'm asked to connect a HP Laserjet 5SiMX to the parallel port of an
> Alpha Station 255 with T64U V 4.0E.
> 
> Are printers supported at the parallel port with this OS version
> (as far as I remember, it wasn't with older versions?!) ?

Thanks to 

Nikola Milutinovic <Nikola.Milutinovic@ev.co.yu>
Ernie LaBonte <labonte@zk3.dec.com>

Ernie explained the way how to use an HP Laserjet 5SiMX at the parallel
port:

  Below is a uuencoded compressed tar file containing the configuration
  files (.pcf) for the HP 5si printer. Copy these files to /usr/lbin/pcf
  and set the file protection to 644 or 444. Create a printcap entry for
  the ln17_a4 printer then change the IF and OF printcap settings to:

	:if=/usr/lbin/pcfof +Chplj5simx_a4.pcf:\
	:of=/usr/lbin/pcfof +Chplj5simx_a4.pcf:\

  If you are using letter paper don't add the _a4 suffix.

And he supplied the necessary pcf-files.

Thanks Ernie
Gerhard

