V4.0 and V4.0E.  I strongly suspect that NONE of our testing verifies
that we haven't done this.

If you have a support contract, report it as a bug and demand a fix.

What I mean by "regress" is that someone made a change somewhere in the kernel
(since autonice is implemented entirely in the kernel) that broke a facility
that was present and working in the system prior to their change, and thus
they introduced a functional regression -- what was working before no longer
works.  It's a bug, plain and simple, ....


