Only one response on this one....
I did a call back from Compaq Support, finally.

Ends up that the SWCC "For Second Controller Option" CD is
just there for it's firmware. The "For Second Controller Option"
just denotes that it came with that kit (semi-guess here). It's still SWCC
V1.0.
And it just so happens, that Compaq Support has emailed me the latest
version - D11V.
AND I just downloaded the latest SWCC version - 2.1 from Compaq's site.
Thanks to Alan Davis for pointing me to a previous summary with the URL.

As far as the "flushing" of the RA3000 controller buffer cache, the
"shutdown"
of the controller, which is part of the Installation Manual instructions
will do that for me.

And YES, I can upgrade the firmware on the controller while in use.
It apparently reads the firmware into memory to run.

I'll post any "gotchas", if there are any...

